1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
hello everyone, today I want to quickly share a tool I developed during my job search

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,380
a small job search tool I coded myself

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,060
returning to the job market this time

4
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:09,980
I feel like the competition is really, really, really fierce

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:11,580
The efficiency is really too low without using AI.

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:12,700
When I was looking for a job myself

7
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,540
often use GPT to help me

8
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:16,660
polish my resume and write some simple cover letters

9
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,940
prepare for interviews, etc.

10
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:19,140
But I often encounter a problem

11
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:20,840
as I apply for more positions

12
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,120
My chat history with GPT becomes extremely long

13
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,440
GPT also starts to lose some context

14
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,100
sometimes it mixes up the information from Job A with the resume for Job B

15
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,120
At this point, I have to explain it all over again

16
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,580
What if I start a new conversation?

17
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:33,240
I have to send the resume again

18
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,960
explain to it what it needs to do

19
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:37,209
Let's take a look at the results first. This is a landing page I created myself.

20
00:00:37,209 --> 00:00:38,209
There are three main features

21
00:00:38,209 --> 00:00:39,969
One is related to applications

22
00:00:39,969 --> 00:00:41,369
such as resumes, cover letters, and so on

23
00:00:41,369 --> 00:00:43,289
The second feature is the automatic parsing of the job description content.

24
00:00:43,289 --> 00:00:44,929
The third is interview preparation

25
00:00:44,929 --> 00:00:48,440
On the Home page, I have also organized everything according to the three stages of job search, application, and interview.

26
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,520
to organize the entry points for all my features

27
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:52,940
Starting from seeing a new job

28
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:54,860
The first step is to upload your resume.

29
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:55,940
Multiple files can be uploaded here

30
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:58,260
Then you can directly paste the JD link here

31
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:00,590
I'll just pick one randomly here

32
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:05,209
Then it will automatically list out some information that I'm particularly interested in

33
00:01:05,209 --> 00:01:06,840
such as salary, identity

34
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,360
What does this company do?

35
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:12,000
some keywords mentioned in the JD that I might not have included in my resume

36
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,440
Because I'm really too lazy to read the JD

37
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,120
and sometimes the job description isn't visible when filling out applications

38
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:17,160
I have to go back and look for it

39
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:20,100
There is a button here that allows you to return to the original link at any time.

40
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,460
Next, we can tailor the resume based on the JD

41
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:24,060
see if the AI has any suggestions

42
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,940
The left side shows the original text of the resume

43
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:28,400
On the right is the wording suggested by the AI for modification

44
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:31,000


45
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,280
or you can regenerate this specific content again

46
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,160
When I first designed it

47
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,000
There is also a resume export function here

48
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,760
But later I realized that I often need to adjust the format based on the content and length of the resume.

49
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,140
Actually, it's still more convenient for me to make adjustments in the original resume file.

50
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:42,940
more convenient

51
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:43,740
I gave up on this feature

52
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,729
and it can also generate a cover letter

53
00:01:45,729 --> 00:01:47,409
generate this cold message

54
00:01:47,409 --> 00:01:48,929
I use it to apply for VC jobs

55
00:01:48,929 --> 00:01:52,160
or jobs that require sending LinkedIn messages or email applications

56
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:55,040
This is most commonly used when filling out applications.

57
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,580
Sometimes there are some custom questions

58
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,560
for example, they might ask you

59
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,840
why do you want to work here

60
00:02:01,139 --> 00:02:03,419
Then the AI will generate a simple answer for me.

61
00:02:03,419 --> 00:02:04,539
When I was working on these features

62
00:02:04,539 --> 00:02:05,539
Actually, I found that as I mentioned in my previous video

63
00:02:05,539 --> 00:02:07,939
simplify job

64
00:02:07,939 --> 00:02:08,299
Visor

65
00:02:08,299 --> 00:02:08,699
Job right

66
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:10,600
It actually has similar functionality

67
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,920
or even when entering a custom question

68
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,380
directly click the button in that input box

69
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:16,460
and generate the answer with one click

70
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,700
but the reason I didn't go in this direction is

71
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,880
One reason is that I think Simplify is already very good at auto fill

72
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,200
I don't need to create another Simplify

73
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:23,560
Secondly,

74
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,840
The Chrome extension is actually a very good use case

75
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,280
because it's right next to the JD

76
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,300
can be used anytime

77
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,300
That's because what I made isn't an auto fill tool

78
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:32,260
so I still need more screen Space

79
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:33,440
to implement other functions

80
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,680
such as the interview preparation section

81
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:37,520
Moreover, the custom question feature of these generation tools

82
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,840
usually require payment to generate

83
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,880
As someone who loves freebies

84
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:42,480
wouldn't be willing to spend this money

85
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,360
Because the model I'm currently using is Ollama

86
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,280
it can run locally on my computer

87
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,180
no need to spend money

88
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:50,160
So this was the original intention behind me wanting to create my own vibe_code tool.

89
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:52,100
OK, the last feature is interview preparation

90
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,420
The existing job records have this type of categorization.

91
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:57,380
You can see whether this job is in the application stage or the interview stage.

92
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,300
For example, I have already received an interview for this job

93
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,780
I can select my interviewer in this tab

94
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:02,880
My interview length

95
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:06,400
You can then choose to have the AI generate interview questions and answers

96
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:09,160
Or I can manually add the questions that I think might be asked

97
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,760
I think the important questions can be added manually

98
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,560
Then let the AI generate this answer for me

99
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,260
So here we'll let the AI generate it

100
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:17,580
Here you will get a set of Q&A answers generated based on the JD

101
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:17,980
then

102
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:20,520
We can also modify or regenerate it ourselves

103
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,460
If you make it to the next round

104
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:23,300
you can also add a new set of questions

105
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,500
Then during the preparation phase

106
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,140
I will enter this practice mode

107
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,940
it will turn into a flash card

108
00:03:27,940 --> 00:03:29,700
I can use it myself to mock an interview

109
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:31,430
As for this product

110
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:33,030
The entire product was designed by myself.

111
00:03:33,030 --> 00:03:36,100
I kind of deliberately used that so-called AI-esque gradient purple color

112
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:37,760
Because I actually quite like this color myself

113
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,640
don't want it to be labeled

114
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:39,880
except to save credits

115
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,120
Occasionally I would tweak the styling myself

116
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:44,420
Otherwise, basically 90% of it was written by Cursor.

117
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:47,800
OK so this is my first complete vibe coding project

118
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:50,600
Because it was basically designed around my own needs

119
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,920
Actually, there are still quite a few imperfections

120
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,880
or compared to directly using large models

121
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:55,240
areas where the advantages are not particularly strong

122
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,920
Currently, it's only something I use locally.

123
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:57,800
If you find it useful

124
